# netsurf: script-inserted scripts are async and fire load / error; flex ignores abspos children
#
# - A <script> that SCRIPT inserted while the document was still parsing was
#   run as a parser-blocking sync script, and the sync path fires neither
#   load nor error; element-recording for load events also required
#   parse_completed. Loaders that insert scripts during parsing -- Google's
#   module loader, YouTube's, webpack chunks -- waited forever. dom_event.c
#   now flags its call (html_script_js_inserted) and such scripts are async
#   (HTML: script-inserted scripts are never parser-blocking), and every
#   external script's element is recorded, so load fires after it runs and
#   error when it fails. YouTube gets past its loading skeleton.
# - flex: an absolutely positioned child is not a flex item (Flexbox 4.1),
#   but its size was subtracted from the free space: two abspos underline
#   bars (width: 100%) beside Google's sign-in field wrapper left its
#   flex-grow nothing -- a 30 px input nobody could tap. Frozen at its own
#   size and left out of the initial and remaining free space.
#
# Test page JS-scriptload.html: 4/4 in tools/run-vita-sim.sh (onload,
# addEventListener load, onerror for a missing file, async = false); with
# the async rule disarmed it reports 0/4.
